 "text": "..title\nA resolution accepting a Child and Adult Care Food Program (CACFP) grant from the Tennessee Department of Human Services to the Metropolitan Government, acting by and through the Metro Nashville Parks and Recreation Department, to provide food program services at 18 Metro Parks community centers. \n..body\nWHEREAS, the Tennessee Department of Human Services has awarded a grant in an amount not to exceed $923,343.00 with no cash match required to the Metropolitan Government, acting by and through the Metro Nashville Parks and Recreation Department, to provide food program services at 18 Metro Parks community centers; and,   \nWHEREAS, it is to the benefit of the citizens of The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County that this grant be accepted.  \nNOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE COUNCIL OF THE METROPOLITAN GOVERNMENT OF NASHVILLE AND DAVIDSON COUNTY:\nSection 1.\tThat the grant by and between the Tennessee Department of Human Services, in an amount not to exceed $923,343.00, to the Metropolitan Government, acting by and through the Metro Nashville Parks and Recreation Department, to provide food program services at 18 Metro Parks community centers, a copy of which is attached hereto and incorporated herein, is hereby approved.    \nSection 2.\tThat the amount of this grant be appropriated to the Metro Nashville Parks and Recreation Department, based on the revenues estimated to be received and any match to be applied.\nSection 3.\tThat this resolution shall take effect from and after its adoption, the welfare of The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County requiring it.\n..Agenda Analysis\nAnalysis\n\nThis resolution accepts a Child and Adult Care Food Program grant from the Tennessee Department of Human Services to the Metro Nashville Parks and Recreation Department (“Metro Parks”) to fund food program services at 18 Metro Parks community centers.\n\nThe grant award is an amount not to exceed $923,343 with no cash match required. The grant term is effective on October 1, 2026, and would end of September 30, 2027.\n\nThe Metropolitan Board of Parks and Recreation accepted this grant at its October 6, 2026 meeting.\n\n"
}
